# What never reaches the build context.
#
# Two jobs. The first is size and speed: the build context is uploaded to the
# daemon before anything runs, so `node_modules/` and `.venv/` alone are most
# of the wait for a build that will not use either.
#
# The second is the one that matters. `.env` holds real database credentials
# and the session signing secret. `COPY . .` is not used in this Dockerfile —
# it copies named directories precisely so a stray file cannot ride along — but
# a `.dockerignore` that omits `.env` is one careless `COPY` away from baking
# credentials into a layer, where they survive deletion in a later layer and
# are readable by anyone who pulls the image.

# ── secrets ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key

# ── build artefacts that must be rebuilt, never copied ───────────────────────
# `client/dist` is produced by stage 1. Copying a local one in would ship
# whatever was last built on somebody's laptop, from a commit nobody recorded.
.venv/
venv/
client/node_modules/
client/dist/
**/__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# ── the project's memory, not its runtime ────────────────────────────────────
# These are why this repository is worth reading and none of them execute in a
# container. `docs/` is ~4MB of specification; `evidence/` holds screenshots.
.git/
.github/
docs/
evidence/
goals/
handoffs/
tests/
workflows/
*.md
!client/public/fonts/README.md

# ── local tooling ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.claude/
.vscode/
.idea/
tools/
alembic/versions/__pycache__/
